  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This 4-star campsite, run by Homair, sits in a valley in Cagnes-sur-Mer, about 5 km from the beaches. It offers mobile homes, a bar-restaurant, a pizzeria, takeaway meals, a small supermarket, a heated swimming pool, entertainment and free wifi at a few access points (bar, restaurant, reception). In high season the reception is open Sunday to Friday from 9am to 12pm and 2pm to 8pm, and Saturday from 9am to 9pm.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The "Services" page of the official website (camping-greenpark.com) says: "Only one dog is allowed per pitch", and adds that your four-legged friend will share your moments at the bar and restaurant. The campsite's Homair listing specifies "one dog allowed (excluding category 1 and 2)" and classes this service as paid; the amount of the supplement is published neither on the campsite website nor on the Homair listing, which only says that a deposit and the tourist tax are paid on site. Category 1 and 2 dogs are excluded.</p>
      <p>The campsite is built in terraces in a valley, with the site open from 2 April to 3 October for the 2027 season according to the header of its website. The reception number is +33 9 77 55 52 74; other directory sites give other numbers, so it is better to stick to the one on the official website.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: only one dog is admitted per pitch, so don't plan to come with two dogs. Ask for the amount of the supplement and any leash rules when you book.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The beaches are about 5 km away, Cagnes-sur-Mer station about 4 to 9 km depending on the sources and Nice airport about ten kilometres, which makes a car useful. The medieval village of Haut-de-Cagnes and the seafront of Cros-de-Cagnes are the nearest outings; no source read specifies whether dogs are accepted on the commune's beaches, ask the town hall or the tourist office.</p>
